                <pb facs="0082" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg2"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lord to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Buenos Ayres</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-07-05"><hi rendition="#italic">July 5,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Lord reports that the Argentine Government has been constrained to declare
                    its capital in a state of siege for a period of six months, owing to public
                    disorder caused by opposition to the bill consolidating the public debt, pending
                    in Congress.</p>
            </div>
